e></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24401859</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC3996700</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/ismej.2013.226</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pii">ismej2013226</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Campbell BJ, Stein JL, Cary SC. Evidence of chemolithoautotrophy in the bacterial community associated with Alvinella pompejana, a hydrothermal vent polychaete. Appl Environ Microbiol. 2003;69:5070&#x2013;5078.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC194926</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">12957888</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Cary SC, Cottrell MT, Stein JL, Camacho F, Desbruyeres D. Molecular identification and localization of filamentous symbiotic bacteria associated with the hydrothermal vent annelid Alvinella pompejana. Appl Environ Microbiol. 1997;63:1124&#x2013;1130.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC1389137</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">16535543</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Chen Y, Dumont MG, McNamara NP, Chamberlain PM, Bodrossy L, Stralis-Pavese N, et al. Diversity of the active methanotrophic community in acidic peatlands as assessed by mRNA and SIP-PLFA analyses. Environ Microbiol. 2008;10:446&#x2013;459.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18093158</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Costello AM, Lidstrom ME. Molecular characterization of functional and phylogenetic genes from natural populations of methanotrophs in lake sediments. Appl Environ Microbiol. 1999;65:5066&#x2013;5074.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC91682</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">10543824</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>de Angelis MA, Baross JA, Lilley MD. Enhanced microbial methane oxidation in water from a deep-sea hydrothermal vent field at simulated in situ hydrostat